177 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 156 0 R
/E (The Challenge :  Oil India already receives real-time drilling telemetry through eRTMAC, while decades of valuable operational knowledge remain distributed across WCRs, DDRs, drilling reports and individual experience. Engineers must manually identify relevant offset-well events, understand the formation/depth context and determine which mitigation worked previously. The challenge is to transform this fragmented knowledge into timely, evidence backed intelligence during active drilling.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
178 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 156 0 R
/E (Proactive risk anticipation. As the active well approaches a formation or depth interval where offset wells experienced stuck pipe, kicks, mud losses or pressure anomalies, the system raises an early warning before the event develops.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
179 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 156 0 R
/E (Institutional memory, not document search. Historical WCRs, DDRs and drilling reports are converted into structured drilling-event records containing well, MD/TVD, formation, event, cause, mitigation and outcome, allowing past experience to become reusable operational knowledge.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
180 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 156 0 R
/E (Subsurface aware well matching, NWIS identifies relevant offset wells using 3D trajectory, TVD and geological formation, rather than relying only on surface distance between wellheads.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
181 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 156 0 R
/E (Live historical intelligence in one pipeline. Real-time parameters such as Torque, Hookload, SPP, ROP, Flow and Pit Volume are continuously correlated with historical events from geologically relevant nearby wells.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
182 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 156 0 R
/E (Open weight models, vector search and predictive ML run inside OIL-controlled infrastructure, with no mandatory public-cloud dependency and support for offline rig-edge operation.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
183 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 156 0 R
/E (Explainability built into every alert. Each alert presents which parameters changed, which historical wells experienced similar conditions, the depth/formation involved, and the mitigation previously applied, instead of generating an opaque AI score.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
